{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg","id":1486350,"title":"Saints and Monsters is on DTRPG!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-13T10:40:36-07:00","id":1486350,"title":"Saints and Monsters is on DTRPG!","content":"I don't have a good quip for this one. <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/402324/Scion-Second-Edition-Players-Guide-Saints--Monsters?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">Go get your Scion on with Saints &amp; Monsters, live on DTRPG</a>.<br /> <br /> Discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T11:34:10-07:00","id":1486355,"title":"","content":"I'm reading through it, and I have a question: Saints can't have Legend, or be Scions or take any Supernatural Paths (without the other players' assent). So how is it that they can be Hero Tier or Demigod Tier? I'm not complaining, mind you; the fact that they <i>can</i> power up is fine by me. I'm just wondering <i>how it happens</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T13:06:21-07:00","id":1486360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg?p=1486355#post1486355\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm reading through it, and I have a question: Saints can't have Legend, or be Scions or take any Supernatural Paths (without the other players' assent). So how is it that they can be Hero Tier or Demigod Tier? I'm not complaining, mind you; the fact that they <i>can</i> power up is fine by me. I'm just wondering <i>how it happens</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>well if they\u2019re in a Band with Scions they move up with the Band, but I\u2019m still trying to figure out what to do if you\u2019re running an all Saints game, etc.<br /> <br /> Edit: I think the Culture Hero rule on page 14 would imply you pay attention to when under Scion rules Legend and Calling dot would be gained, and the Saint still gains a Calling dot at the appropriate point, so you move up a tier at the same point of growth paying attention to that as a Scion would, even without Legend.<br /> <br /> i will make a note in errata that this can use clarification","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-13-2022, 05:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T17:28:15-07:00","id":1486379,"title":"","content":"Anyone have any idea of how many Edge points you would have if you're allowing them in addition to Birthrights? Like Trinity - 2 per path?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T22:16:27-07:00","id":1486388,"title":"","content":"As I understand you get them instead of birthrights in the last step of character creation, 1 dot for 1 dot, or with XP for 5 XP per dot.<br /> <br /> To be fair it just compare it to birthrights, it don\u2019t say how to buy them\u2026 but it\u2019s how I understand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-13T23:58:10-07:00","id":1486390,"title":"","content":"Okay, Saints are INTENSE - everything they do is about their Virtue and being Virtuous! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Prophets are much more like Acanthus from <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> - or Muad'Dib from Dune...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T10:08:28-07:00","id":1486439,"title":"","content":"I was disappointed that this was all rules and no lore (especially for sorcerers). But I guess what can you expect from a Players Guide?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:08:51-07:00","id":1486447,"title":"","content":"Apologies if this has already been answered, but is there an errata sheet for the book? I found an error when reviewing the sorcerer section that I think needs to be reported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T11:50:27-07:00","id":1486454,"title":"","content":"Check for an email from dtrpg for the purchase. The link is in there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-14T13:53:25-07:00","id":1486461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg?p=1486388#post1486388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I understand you get them instead of birthrights in the last step of character creation, 1 dot for 1 dot, or with XP for 5 XP per dot.<br /> <br /> To be fair it just compare it to birthrights, it don\u2019t say how to buy them\u2026 but it\u2019s how I understand.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it\u2019s just it says \u201cinstead of, or in addition to\u201d, so you can play with both Birthrights and Edges. I suppose just using the same creation and XP rules for both works well, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5619-starkjunior","name":"StarkJunior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-17T23:47:15-07:00","id":1486847,"title":"","content":"I have noticed something : the section about the new Calling &quot;Outsider&quot; mentions Circe, the famous greek magician of the Odyssey. Yet, i don't thing a book of Scion, including this one, talked about her. Am i wrong and missing something, or do you all think this is some kind of foreshadowing of a future release ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T01:08:50-07:00","id":1486853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lady Darcia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg?p=1486847#post1486847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have noticed something : the section about the new Calling &quot;Outsider&quot; mentions Circe, the famous greek magician of the Odyssey. Yet, i don't thing a book of Scion, including this one, talked about her. Am i wrong and missing something, or do you all think this is some kind of foreshadowing of a future release ?</div> </div> </div> </div>She is referenced as a Scion of Hecate in Mysteries of the World.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-18T23:39:24-07:00","id":1486968,"title":"","content":"Ah, thank you ! I was wondering if she had a full description like Gods do somewhere, with all three Callings and Purviews, but this should be a nice foundation for a GM to build on. Thanks again !","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sorry i am french ;__;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27418-lady-darcia","name":"Lady Darcia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27418_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T02:49:35-07:00","id":1487139,"title":"","content":"I don't like reading rpg books as pdfs, so I'm waiting for the pod version. Can someone who has the book give a list of the included denizen options, and are there rules for demigod level denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/706-rickayelm","name":"rickayelm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"76"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T07:15:11-07:00","id":1487186,"title":"","content":"Humanoid Denizens: Animal Headed Creatures; Fair Folk, Hidden Folk, and Little Folk; Giant; Underfolk; Water Spirit; Winged. <br /> <br /> Partially Humanoid Denizens: Centaur, Lamia, Motorcycle Centaur, and Nuckelavee. <br /> <br /> Nonhumanoid Denizens: Sphinx, Lamassu, Komainu/Shisa/Shishi; Magical Animals Who Really Shouldn't Be; Rakshasa. <br /> <br /> And no, there's nothing on Demigod level Denizens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-20T09:04:42-07:00","id":1487201,"title":"","content":"Nothing stops non-Scion Denizen PCs from proceeding past Legend 4, but as written they don\u2019t get any additional enhancements for doing so, so unless they are Scions in their own right they will be progressively falling further behind equal Legend Scions as the latter approaches Godhood.<br /> <br /> the trade-off being they aren\u2019t on a \u201capotheosis or death\u201d run. Legendary Denizens can comfortably sit at Legend 8 chilling for centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 07-20-2022, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T03:41:30-07:00","id":1487857,"title":"","content":"I'm reading the Lifepath System for creating Adolecent characters, and it says they don't have a Role Path. They do however have both their Origin Path and their Pantheon Path. It seems they only get Life Events from their Origin Path. Does that mean they get zero skill points from their Pantheon Path? Or if they do get skill points from their Pantheon Path as well how many do they get? 2 dots of each seems to be in line with the old rules, but I can't see it mentioned anywhere.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found the answer on p. 130. You get 2 dots in each skill of your Pantheon Path...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13122,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13122-mordekain","user":"Mordekain","date":". 07-25-2022, 07:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13122-mordekain","name":"Mordekain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T13:46:45-07:00","id":1488205,"title":"","content":"In Saints and Monsters there are variations on when characters get specialties to their skills. For example Saints and Prophets get them at skill level 3 and up and they also get them if the skill is raised with the dots from final touches while Denizen characters creation gives specialties to skills above 3, so at three is not enough, and specifically says that the dots added on final touches do not grant specialties even if they raise the score to 4 of above.<br /> <br /> Are these differences intentional or a mistake?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T13:49:56-07:00","id":1488206,"title":"","content":"Also, since Denizens have no callings how many Knacks can they have active at the same time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:08:53-07:00","id":1488209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg?p=1488206#post1488206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, since Denizens have no callings how many Knacks can they have active at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>The implication seems to be that Legendary Denizens (i.e. not Scions, Saints, Prophets, or Magicians - just Denizens with Legend) have all their purchased Knacks active.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:37:54-07:00","id":1488211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1486350-saints-and-monsters-is-on-dtrpg?p=1488209#post1488209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The implication seems to be that Legendary Denizens (i.e. not Scions, Saints, Prophets, or Magicians - just Denizens with Legend) have all their purchased Knacks active.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was my impression as well. If it is so then consider me happy since switching Knacks around has been one of my major annoyances in Scion. That alone is a reason to consider playing Denizens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://foru